# Round 57: pins the first-use CLOSURE's acceptance. The writer `seta` is
# never mentioned at the top level -- only `viab` is -- so before the
# closure its first-use was null and the demoted arm refused this VALID
# program (measured: over-broad eviction). The closure propagates viab's
# top-level first-use to seta through the body-mention graph; the module
# binding (v is 1) provably precedes it, so outward routing is sound and
# the write must reach the module binding exactly as the VM's does.
v is 1
define seta(k) as:
    v is v + k
    return 0
define viab(k) as:
    x is seta of k
    return 0
y is viab of 4
print of v
v is "s"
print of v
